l Laboratory is operated for DOE by Battelle Memorial Institute under contract DE-AC05-76RLO 1830. In addition, Ottmar Mohler, Naruki Hiranuma and Gourihar Kulkarni acknowledge the EMSL general use grant (proposal ID 49077) for supporting the PNNLCIC work. The BINARY group (Carsten Budke, Evelyn Jantsch and Thomas Koop) acknowledges funding from DFG under the INUIT subproject KO 2944/2-2 and also acknowledges Sabine Robrecht, who designed and performed experiments that contributed to the development of the recommended suspension preparation protocol. The CMU-CS team (Michael Polen, Hassan Beydoun, and Ryan C. Sullivan) was supported by the National Science Foundation (grant number CHE-1554941, and a graduate research fellowship for Michael Polen). The NIPR-CRAFT experiments were partly supported by JSPS KAKENHI grant numbers 15K13570 and 16H06020. Kimberly M. Cory and Naruki Hiranuma thank the NSF-EAPSI for the validation of NCC as well as microscopy characterization of our cellulose samples conducted in collaboration with Yutaka Tobo and Kouji Adachi in Japan. The Leeds group thanks the European Research Council (ERC, 240449 ICE; 632272 IceControl; 648661; MarineIce; 713664 CryoProtect) and the Natural Environment Research Council (NERC, NE/I019057/1). The part of the research based on LINDA measurements was supported by the Swiss National Science Foundation (SNF) through grant nos. 200021\_140228 and 200020\_159194. For M-AL and M-WT, Miklos Szakall and Amelie Mayer acknowledge support from Deutsche Forschungsgemeinschaft (DFG) under contract SZ260/4-2 within Research Unit INUIT (FOR 1525). The NC State group (Hans Taylor and Markus D. Petters) acknowledges funding from NSF-AGS 1450690. The NC State group thanks Danielle Dillane, Mary Hester, Chris Rohrbach, Margaret Scott, Hannah Tekleab and Mark Wu for their help with collecting the raw data. The WISDOM team (Yinon Rudich and Naama Reicher) gratefully acknowledge support from the Ice Nuclei Research Unit (INUIT)